From bf64ba1cdd0def8842b757ca8430731a71fc6cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thesis Assistant <thesis-bot@local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 06:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove train-split scoring/reporting; train only trains the
 AE

- train.py: stop scoring the train split, only train the autoencoder on
  normal-only images (normal_loader). Threshold selection and all reported
  metrics/artifacts now come only from val and test.
- io_utils.SPLITS: ('train','val','test') -> ('val','test'), the single
  source of truth for which splits get scored/saved/loaded.
- visualize.py: drop all references to the train split (EDA, ROC/PR,
  confusion matrix, score distribution, heatmaps, galleries).
- visual.py: plot_class_distribution/plot_roc_curves/plot_pr_curves/
  plot_confusion_matrices/plot_score_distributions no longer hardcode
  plt.subplots(1, 3, ...) - subplot count now adapts to len(split_meta)
  so there is no empty subplot now that only val/test are reported.

Note: scan_and_split()/build_datasets_and_loaders() still compute a train
split internally (needed to filter out the normal-only subset used to
train the AE) - only the downstream scoring/reporting of that split was
removed.
